('salexpa','Carcinoma ex pleomorphic adenoma','A retained PLAG1/HMGA2 event can reveal the precursor.','Progression — TP53 and other carcinoma-type alterations','Progression subset — ERBB2 amplification','Precursor-associated — PLAG1 or HMGA2 rearrangement','Carcinoma type determines additional drivers; the precursor rearrangement alone does not prove malignant transformation.','sal'),
('salintraduct','Intraductal carcinoma of salivary gland','Intraductal salivary carcinoma can be RET-fusion driven.','Apocrine subset — HRAS, PIK3CA','','Subset — NCOA4::RET, TRIM27::RET and alternative kinase fusions','Most are indolent/intraductal; only malignant/invasive context is included, and fusion alone does not establish invasion.','sal'),
('salmicro','Microsecretory adenocarcinoma','Microsecretory → MEF2C::SS18.','','','Characteristic — MEF2C::SS18','Distinct from SS18::SSX synovial sarcoma.','sal'),
('salscler','Sclerosing microcystic adenocarcinoma','A rare salivary carcinoma without a reliable genetic hallmark.','','','','Do not infer the genotype of cutaneous microcystic adnexal carcinoma from resemblance.','sal'),
('salmucin','Mucinous adenocarcinoma of salivary gland','Salivary mucinous carcinoma → AKT1 E17K in subsets.','Recurrent — AKT1 E17K','','','Papillary/colloid/signet-ring patterns grouped. Exclude metastasis.','sal'),
('salbasal','Basal cell adenocarcinoma of salivary gland','Salivary basal cell malignancy has variable WNT biology.','Subset — CTNNB1/CYLD-pathway alterations','','','A basal phenotype does not imply the PTCH1 pathway of skin BCC.','sal'),
('sallymph','Lymphoepithelial carcinoma of salivary gland','Salivary lymphoepithelial carcinoma may be EBV-driven.','','','','EBV association is geographically variable; exclude a nasopharyngeal primary.','sal'),
('salnos','Salivary carcinoma, NOS','NOS is an exclusion category without a single driver.','','','','Includes rare unclassified adenocarcinoma and carcinoma patterns; revisit molecularly defined entities first.','sal'),
